# Modus Colors - Essential Rules

## ✅ ALWAYS Use Design System Colors

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Tailwind classes with design system colors
<div className="bg-background text-foreground">
<div className="bg-card text-card-foreground">
<div className="bg-primary text-primary-foreground">
<div className="text-muted-foreground">
```

## ✅ Modus Web Components Use Color Props

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Built-in color props
<ModusWcButton color="primary">Button</ModusWcButton>
<ModusWcButton color="secondary">Button</ModusWcButton>
<ModusWcButton color="danger">Button</ModusWcButton>
```

## ❌ NEVER Use These

```tsx
// ❌ FORBIDDEN - Will be flagged by linter
className="bg-blue-500 text-red-400"
style={{ backgroundColor: "#ffffff" }}
style={{ color: "rgb(255, 255, 255)" }}
style={{ backgroundColor: "var(--modus-wc-color-base-page)" }}
```

## 🎯 Key Pattern

- **Custom UI**: Use Tailwind classes (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`)
- **Modus Components**: Use color props (`color="primary"`)
- **Never**: Hardcoded colors, raw Modus variables, Tailwind color classes

